Under Article I of the GATS, trade in services is defined as the supply of a service through the following four modes:

(a) "from the territory of one Member into the territory of any other Member" [GATS Art. I];
(b) "in the territory of one Member to the service consumer of any other Member" [GATS Art. I];
(c) "by a service supplier of one Member, through commercial presence in the territory of any other Member" [GATS Art. I];
(d) "by a service supplier of one Member, through presence of natural persons of a Member in the territory of any other Member" [GATS Art. I].
